{"module":"technology","voice":"male","duration":215.9,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Technology and AI: old bias in new code","start":0.0,"end":4.01,"words":[[0.05,1.01],[1.01,1.3],[1.3,1.78],[2.12,2.5],[2.5,2.99],[2.99,3.18],[3.18,3.47],[3.47,3.85]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Algorithms learn from data, and the data carry history.","start":4.81,"end":8.85,"words":[[4.86,5.57],[5.57,5.78],[5.78,6.06],[6.06,6.49],[6.74,6.95],[6.95,7.09],[7.09,7.45],[7.45,7.73],[7.73,8.3]]},{"el":"intro","text":"A system trained on past arrests learns where police patrolled; one trained on past spending learns who got care.","start":9.2,"end":16.08,"words":[[9.24,9.38],[9.38,9.83],[9.83,10.27],[10.27,10.42],[10.42,10.71],[10.71,11.15],[11.15,11.45],[11.45,11.67],[11.67,12.04],[12.04,12.7],[12.96,13.18],[13.18,13.62],[13.62,13.77],[13.77,14.07],[14.07,14.58],[14.58,14.88],[14.88,15.03],[15.03,15.25],[15.25,15.54]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Technology can also expose bias, if people insist on testing it.","start":16.43,"end":21.32,"words":[[16.48,17.22],[17.22,17.44],[17.44,17.8],[17.8,18.32],[18.32,18.76],[19.02,19.16],[19.16,19.53],[19.53,19.97],[19.97,20.12],[20.12,20.56],[20.56,20.78]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Risk scores in the courtroom","start":21.67,"end":23.65,"words":[[21.71,22.09],[22.09,22.48],[22.48,22.67],[22.67,22.86],[22.86,23.43]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Many courts use software to predict whether a defendant will reoffend.","start":24.35,"end":29.02,"words":[[24.4,24.71],[24.71,25.01],[25.01,25.23],[25.23,25.76],[25.76,25.91],[25.91,26.44],[26.44,26.74],[26.74,26.89],[26.89,27.57],[27.57,27.8],[27.8,28.48]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 2016 ProPublica analyzed one tool, COMPAS, in Broward County, Florida, and found that Black defendants who did not reoffend were nearly twice as likely as white defendants to have been labeled high risk.","start":29.37,"end":43.36,"words":[[29.42,29.57],[29.57,30.5],[30.5,31.3],[31.3,31.88],[31.88,32.09],[32.09,32.38],[32.64,33.14],[33.39,33.54],[33.54,33.97],[33.97,34.48],[34.73,35.31],[35.56,35.78],[35.78,36.14],[36.14,36.36],[36.36,36.65],[36.65,37.37],[37.37,37.51],[37.51,37.73],[37.73,37.95],[37.95,38.52],[38.52,38.67],[38.67,39.03],[39.03,39.39],[39.39,39.54],[39.54,39.97],[39.97,40.11],[40.11,40.4],[40.4,41.13],[41.13,41.27],[41.27,41.49],[41.49,41.7],[41.7,42.21],[42.21,42.43],[42.43,42.79]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The company answered that its scores were equally accurate for both groups.","start":43.71,"end":48.45,"words":[[43.76,43.92],[43.92,44.49],[44.49,44.89],[44.89,45.13],[45.13,45.37],[45.37,45.69],[45.69,45.85],[45.85,46.34],[46.34,46.9],[46.9,47.06],[47.06,47.38],[47.38,47.87]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Computer scientists then proved that when two groups have different arrest rates, a tool can't satisfy both definitions of fairness at once.","start":48.8,"end":57.8,"words":[[48.85,49.46],[49.46,50.22],[50.22,50.45],[50.45,50.83],[50.83,51.06],[51.06,51.29],[51.29,51.44],[51.44,51.82],[51.82,52.05],[52.05,52.59],[52.59,52.97],[52.97,53.43],[53.69,53.85],[53.85,54.08],[54.08,54.38],[54.38,54.99],[54.99,55.3],[55.3,56.06],[56.06,56.21],[56.21,56.67],[56.67,56.82],[56.82,57.21]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Which definition should win is still debated.","start":58.15,"end":60.76,"words":[[58.2,58.44],[58.44,58.98],[58.98,59.16],[59.16,59.34],[59.34,59.46],[59.46,59.7],[59.7,60.25]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Ads and search","start":61.66,"end":62.85,"words":[[61.7,61.98],[61.98,62.27],[62.27,62.66]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In 2013, Harvard professor Latanya Sweeney found that searching for names more common among Black Americans was more likely to bring up ads suggesting an arrest record.","start":63.55,"end":74.76,"words":[[63.59,63.76],[63.76,64.73],[65.01,65.42],[65.42,65.98],[65.98,66.55],[66.55,66.95],[66.95,67.36],[67.36,67.6],[67.6,68.09],[68.09,68.25],[68.25,68.66],[68.66,68.82],[68.82,69.22],[69.22,69.55],[69.55,69.87],[69.87,70.6],[70.6,70.84],[70.84,71.0],[71.0,71.49],[71.49,71.65],[71.65,71.98],[71.98,72.14],[72.14,72.38],[72.38,73.11],[73.11,73.27],[73.27,73.68],[73.68,74.16]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In 2022, Meta settled a Justice Department lawsuit alleging its ad-delivery system steered housing ads by race and other protected traits, and agreed to change it.","start":75.11,"end":86.52,"words":[[75.16,75.31],[75.31,76.42],[76.68,76.97],[76.97,77.42],[77.42,77.56],[77.56,78.08],[78.08,78.75],[78.75,79.12],[79.12,79.64],[79.64,79.86],[79.86,80.6],[80.6,81.05],[81.05,81.42],[81.42,81.86],[81.86,82.08],[82.08,82.3],[82.3,82.6],[82.6,82.82],[82.82,83.05],[83.05,83.71],[83.71,84.23],[84.49,84.71],[84.71,85.08],[85.08,85.23],[85.23,85.75],[85.75,85.97]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Hiring and health","start":87.42,"end":88.79,"words":[[87.46,88.06],[88.06,88.31],[88.31,88.66]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Amazon scrapped an experimental hiring tool in 2018 after finding it penalized résumés that included the word “women's,” because it had learned from a decade of mostly male hires.","start":89.49,"end":101.47,"words":[[89.54,90.0],[90.0,90.45],[90.45,90.61],[90.61,91.59],[91.59,92.13],[92.13,92.36],[92.36,92.51],[92.51,93.42],[93.42,93.73],[93.73,94.26],[94.26,94.41],[94.41,95.1],[95.1,95.71],[95.71,95.93],[95.93,96.54],[96.54,96.7],[96.7,96.92],[96.92,97.46],[97.46,97.84],[97.84,97.99],[97.99,98.22],[98.22,98.52],[98.52,98.83],[98.83,98.98],[98.98,99.44],[99.44,99.59],[99.59,100.12],[100.12,100.43],[100.43,100.88]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The same mechanism can encode race.","start":101.82,"end":104.49,"words":[[101.86,102.0],[102.0,102.29],[102.29,102.94],[102.94,103.16],[103.16,103.59],[103.59,103.95]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A health algorithm used on millions of patients underestimated Black patients' needs (see “Is racism over?”).","start":104.84,"end":112.18,"words":[[104.89,105.05],[105.05,105.36],[105.36,106.06],[106.06,106.38],[106.38,106.53],[106.53,107.08],[107.08,107.24],[107.24,107.86],[107.86,109.03],[109.03,109.35],[109.35,109.97],[109.97,110.29],[110.29,110.44],[110.44,110.6],[110.6,111.22],[111.22,111.61]]},{"el":"s2","text":"New York City has required bias audits of automated hiring tools since 2023.","start":112.53,"end":118.64,"words":[[112.58,112.8],[112.8,113.03],[113.03,113.33],[113.33,113.55],[113.55,114.15],[114.15,114.52],[114.52,114.89],[114.89,115.04],[115.04,115.72],[115.72,116.24],[116.24,116.54],[116.54,116.84],[116.84,118.03]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Sensors and predictions","start":119.54,"end":121.27,"words":[[119.59,120.06],[120.06,120.3],[120.3,121.1]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Chicago's inspector general found in 2021 that few ShotSpotter gunshot alerts led police to evidence of a gun crime, while the sensors were concentrated in Black and Latino neighborhoods, sending officers into those streets on high alert.","start":121.97,"end":138.44,"words":[[122.01,122.65],[122.65,123.29],[123.29,123.93],[123.93,124.34],[124.34,124.5],[124.5,125.7],[125.7,125.94],[125.94,126.18],[126.18,126.83],[126.83,127.31],[127.31,127.71],[127.71,127.95],[127.95,128.35],[128.35,128.51],[128.51,129.08],[129.08,129.24],[129.24,129.4],[129.4,129.64],[129.64,130.12],[130.4,130.72],[130.72,130.89],[130.89,131.37],[131.37,131.53],[131.53,132.57],[132.57,132.73],[132.73,133.06],[133.06,133.3],[133.3,133.86],[133.86,134.66],[134.94,135.43],[135.43,135.91],[135.91,136.23],[136.23,136.55],[136.55,137.03],[137.03,137.19],[137.19,137.44],[137.44,137.84]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Chicago ended its contract in 2024.","start":138.79,"end":142.4,"words":[[138.81,139.34],[139.34,139.72],[139.72,139.95],[139.95,140.56],[140.56,140.71],[140.71,141.85]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Predictive policing tools face similar criticism (see “Surveillance”).","start":142.75,"end":147.64,"words":[[142.8,143.53],[143.53,144.1],[144.1,144.42],[144.42,144.75],[144.75,145.23],[145.23,146.04],[146.04,146.2],[146.2,147.02]]},{"el":"h4","text":"AI image generators","start":148.54,"end":150.51,"words":[[148.59,148.94],[148.94,149.37],[149.37,150.32]]},{"el":"s4","text":"A 2023 Bloomberg analysis of thousands of images made by the Stable Diffusion generator found that prompts for high-paying jobs mostly produced lighter-skinned men, while prompts like “inmate” mostly produced people with darker skin, exaggerating real-world disparities.","start":151.21,"end":168.65,"words":[[151.26,151.41],[151.41,152.48],[152.48,152.91],[152.91,153.48],[153.48,153.63],[153.63,154.2],[154.2,154.34],[154.34,154.85],[154.85,155.13],[155.13,155.35],[155.35,155.49],[155.49,155.99],[155.99,156.57],[156.57,157.28],[157.28,157.64],[157.64,157.86],[157.86,158.36],[158.36,158.5],[158.5,159.07],[159.07,159.43],[159.43,159.93],[159.93,160.51],[160.51,161.22],[161.22,161.51],[161.76,162.05],[162.05,162.55],[162.55,162.84],[162.84,163.27],[163.27,163.77],[163.77,164.34],[164.34,164.7],[164.7,164.92],[164.92,165.2],[165.2,165.56],[165.81,166.74],[166.74,167.32],[167.32,168.1]]},{"el":"s4","text":"As AI images spread, they can reinforce the same stereotypes that make someone look “suspicious.”","start":169.0,"end":175.37,"words":[[169.04,169.18],[169.18,169.47],[169.47,169.97],[169.97,170.4],[170.65,170.87],[170.87,171.08],[171.08,171.66],[171.66,171.8],[171.8,172.09],[172.09,173.02],[173.02,173.23],[173.23,173.52],[173.52,173.95],[173.95,174.16],[174.16,174.81]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Making technology accountable","start":176.27,"end":178.39,"words":[[176.32,176.76],[176.76,177.48],[177.48,178.2]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Test before trusting: require independent bias audits and publish the results, as New York City now does for hiring tools.","start":179.09,"end":187.71,"words":[[179.14,179.45],[179.45,179.76],[179.76,180.39],[180.67,181.22],[181.22,182.08],[182.08,182.47],[182.47,182.86],[182.86,183.1],[183.1,183.57],[183.57,183.72],[183.72,184.35],[184.63,184.78],[184.78,185.02],[185.02,185.25],[185.25,185.57],[185.57,185.8],[185.8,186.04],[186.04,186.2],[186.2,186.74],[186.74,187.14]]},{"el":"s5","text":"A human decides: no arrest, sentence, loan or benefit decision by algorithm alone, and a right to appeal to a person.","start":188.06,"end":197.07,"words":[[188.1,188.26],[188.26,188.72],[188.72,189.34],[189.61,189.84],[189.84,190.31],[190.58,191.19],[191.47,191.77],[191.77,191.85],[191.85,192.39],[192.39,192.93],[192.93,193.17],[193.17,193.86],[193.86,194.32],[194.6,194.83],[194.83,194.98],[194.98,195.29],[195.29,195.45],[195.45,195.75],[195.75,195.91],[195.91,196.06],[196.06,196.53]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Transparency: people should be told when an automated system scored them.","start":197.42,"end":202.95,"words":[[197.47,198.53],[198.81,199.22],[199.22,199.46],[199.46,199.63],[199.63,200.03],[200.03,200.27],[200.27,200.44],[200.44,201.17],[201.17,201.66],[201.66,201.98],[201.98,202.31]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Local control: require city council approval before police buy surveillance technology, as some cities' “Community Control Over Police Surveillance” ordinances do.","start":203.3,"end":214.96,"words":[[203.35,203.84],[203.84,204.57],[204.85,205.42],[205.42,205.74],[205.74,206.31],[206.31,206.88],[206.88,207.2],[207.2,207.61],[207.61,207.85],[207.85,208.58],[208.58,209.47],[209.76,209.92],[209.92,210.16],[210.16,210.57],[210.57,211.3],[211.3,211.95],[211.95,212.27],[212.27,212.67],[212.67,213.4],[213.4,214.13],[214.13,214.38]]}]}